Now, leaving aside, things we know about problems of access, like broadband access and things like that, but just looking developmentally at the question, the committee weighed the ways that students can engage in virtual learning as it relates to their development. So young children in particular are still in the process of developing self-regulation, executive function, all the things that allow you to monitor and check on your own learning. Maintaining attention, diverting your attention back if you get distracted, things like that. Young children are less able to do that than older children. On the whole, certainly there's wide individual differences.
撇开我们已知的接入问题（如宽带接入等）不谈，仅从发展角度来看，委员会权衡了学生参与虚拟学习的方式与其发展之间的关系。特别是年幼的孩子，他们仍处于发展自我调节、执行功能以及所有允许你监控和检查自己学习过程的能力的阶段。保持注意力、在分心时将注意力拉回等。与大孩子相比，年幼的孩子在这方面的能力较弱。总的来说，当然存在广泛的个体差异。

