00:05:53.000 --> 00:06:46.000
the home. There may not be older children or older children may need to do their own virtual learning. We can't assume that all young children are going to have that support. And so there was a real worry about that. On top of that, there is well-established evidence that for kids in kindergarten through third grade, particularly in reading but also in mathematics, If you have delays in those early grades, and for example, you don't get to a certain level in your reading proficiency, it can have long-term consequences for your academic success. So that the turn of phrase is that up to third grade, you learn to read. After third grade, you read to learn. And so that if you haven't developed some sort of proficiency in reading, by then, you tend to get farther and farther behind.
家。家里可能没有年长的孩子，或者年长的孩子也需要进行自己的虚拟学习。我们不能假设所有年幼的孩子都能得到这种支持。因此，这确实令人担忧。此外，有充分的证据表明，对于幼儿园到三年级的孩子，特别是在阅读和数学方面，如果你在这些早期年级出现滞后，例如，阅读能力没有达到一定水平，可能会对你的学业成功产生长期影响。所以有一句俗语是：三年级之前，你学习阅读；三年级之后，你通过阅读来学习。因此，如果你在那之前没有培养出某种阅读能力，你往往会越来越落后。

