00:08:23.000 --> 00:09:09.000
as you move into middle school and especially into high school, kids are developing what we call executive function, the ability to monitor their own learning, the ability to regulate their own behavior and regulate attention. So it's what we might call metacognition, the ability to kind of look at your own state of knowledge, to understand your memory limitations, to know when your attention is drifting and have strategies for bringing it back. And that develops over time. And starting in middle school and into high school, kids are getting better at that. Certainly, they still have a ways to go. Those of us who know middle schoolers and high schoolers know they're not all great at it, but they're certainly getting better and you see a big difference between, say, a seven-year-old
当你进入初中，尤其是高中时，孩子们正在发展我们所说的执行功能，即监控自己学习的能力，调节自己行为和注意力的能力。这可能被称为元认知，即审视自己知识状态的能力，了解自己记忆的局限性，知道自己的注意力何时漂移并有策略地将其拉回。这是随着时间推移而发展的。从初中到高中，孩子们在这方面做得越来越好。当然，他们还有很长的路要走。我们这些了解初中生和高中生的人都知道，他们并非都擅长此道，但他们确实在进步，而且你可以看到，比如七岁

